From 1c9d7cb6f61e49c05753ece4413fed231bf7be85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josua Mayer <josua@solid-run.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:37:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] phy: lynx-28g: keep link training defaults when the
 lane mode is unchanged

lynx_28g_set_link_mode() always created a new link training algorithm,
which reads its default TX equalization from the lane registers. But
lynx_28g_set_lane_mode() returns early when the lane mode does not change
(e.g. 10GBase-KR -> 10GBase-KR on every link down/up), so the protocol
configuration table is not reapplied, and the "defaults" become the
coefficients left behind by the previous training session. Each training
then starts from wherever the last one ended.

Match the behaviour of lynx_28g_set_mode() on the net-phy-upstreaming
branch of Vladimir Oltean (github.com/vladimiroltean/linux), which only
creates the algorithm, and reads its defaults, when the lane mode actually
changes.

Signed-off-by: Josua Mayer <josua@solid-run.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-28g.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-28g.c b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-28g.c
index 7c053b40e3bd..cf8d54e2c397 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-28g.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-28g.c
@@ -1780,10 +1780,21 @@ static int lynx_28g_set_link_mode(struct phy *phy,
 				  enum ethtool_link_mode_bit_indices submode)
 {
 	struct lynx_28g_lane *lane = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	enum lynx_28g_lane_mode lane_mode = link_mode_to_lane_mode(submode);
 	struct lynx_xgkr_algorithm *algorithm;
 	int err;
 
-	err = lynx_28g_set_lane_mode(phy, link_mode_to_lane_mode(submode));
+	/* The link training algorithm captures its default TX equalization
+	 * from the registers, right after lynx_28g_set_lane_mode() programmed
+	 * them from the protocol configuration table. If the lane mode is not
+	 * changing, the table is not applied again, and the registers hold
+	 * whatever the previous training session left behind. Keep the
+	 * existing algorithm and its defaults in that case.
+	 */
+	if (lane_mode == lane->mode && lane->algorithm)
+		return 0;
+
+	err = lynx_28g_set_lane_mode(phy, lane_mode);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
